   "title": "How to use",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "OLD PHOTO RESTORE (2 passes, gentle)\n\n1. Load the old photo.\n2. Press Run (about 3 minutes on 6 GB).\n\nPass 1 rebuilds the damage in black and white. Pass 2 adds colour starting FROM the repaired photo (denoise 0.6), so faces can't drift.\nTested on a 1914 photo: the full-strength speed LoRA looked crunchy and HDR; 30 steps without it gave a different face; this recipe looked like a real photo (softer, hand-tinted colour).\nTip: name colours you know in the pass 2 prompt.\n\n6 GB settings (tested on a 6 GB graphics card with 16 GB of RAM): int8 model and text encoder, the 8-step speed LoRA (8 steps, CFG 1, deis_2m: needs the RES4LYF nodes; or pick euler), comfy kitchen attention, pictures scaled to 1 MP. First run of the day is slower while the files load.\nLicence: Qwen Image 2.1 is under the Qwen Research License (non-commercial)."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "OLD PHOTO RESTORE (2 passes, gentle)\n\n1. Load the old photo.\n2. Press Run (about 3 minutes on 6 GB).\n\nPass 1 rebuilds the damage in black and white. Pass 2 adds colour starting FROM the repaired photo (denoise 0.6), so faces can't drift.\nTested on a 1914 photo: the full-strength speed LoRA looked crunchy and HDR; 30 steps without it gave a different face; this recipe looked like a real photo (softer, hand-tinted colour).\nTip: name colours you know in the pass 2 prompt.\n\n6 GB settings (tested on a 6 GB graphics card with 16 GB of RAM): int8 model and text encoder, the 8-step speed LoRA (8 steps, CFG 1, deis_2m: needs the RES4LYF nodes; or pick euler), comfy kitchen attention, pictures scaled to 1 MP. First run of the day is slower while the files load.\nLicence: Qwen Image 2.1 is under the Qwen Research License (non-commercial)."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
